From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: babarot <b4b4r07@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:36:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Add ui.toast.dismiss_on_read to close a space's toasts once
 it is opened

An in-app toast closes only when its duration runs out or when it is
clicked, so with ui.toast.duration_seconds = 0 a toast stays up after
its space was opened from the sidebar and its agents were read there.

ui.toast.dismiss_on_read closes the toasts of a space once that space
is opened, from the sidebar or by keyboard, whatever the duration. Only
that space's toasts close: a linked worktree is its own space, so
opening it leaves the toasts of its parent and sibling worktrees, and
of other machines, stacked. A space opened while the terminal is in the
background is not read, so its toasts close when the terminal regains
focus. A toast that arrives later from another tab of the open space
stays until another space is opened and this one again. It is off by
default, so nothing changes for existing configs.
